  "exercisePushS1WallPushupName": "Wall Push-up",
  "exercisePushS1WallPushupDesc": "Stand a step away from the wall and press your palms at chest height. Bend your arms until your chest touches the wall, then push back.",
  "exercisePushS1WallPushupTip": "Keep your body straight — don't arch your lower back.",
  "exercisePushS2KneePushupName": "Knee Push-up",
  "exercisePushS2KneePushupDesc": "Push-up position with knees on the floor. Keep a straight line from knees to head. Lower your chest to the floor, then press up.",
  "exercisePushS2KneePushupTip": "Don't drop your hips — keep a straight line from knees to shoulders.",
  "exercisePushS3FullPushupName": "Full Push-up",
  "exercisePushS3FullPushupDesc": "Classic push-up position. Body forms a straight line from heels to head. Chest touches or comes within 2–3 cm of the floor.",
  "exercisePushS3FullPushupTip": "Brace your core and glutes to keep your hips from sagging.",
  "exercisePushS4DiamondPushupName": "Diamond Push-up",
  "exercisePushS4DiamondPushupDesc": "Hands under your chest with thumbs and index fingers forming a diamond. Targets the triceps. Keep elbows tucked on the way down.",
  "exercisePushS4DiamondPushupTip": "Don't flare your elbows — let them glide along your body.",
  "exercisePushS5WidePushupName": "Wide Push-up",
  "exercisePushS5WidePushupDesc": "Hands placed significantly wider than shoulder-width. Lower slowly while keeping your body in a straight line. Both chest and triceps work through a wide range of motion.",
  "exercisePushS5WidePushupTip": "The wider your hands, the more the chest is targeted and the less the triceps.",
  "exercisePushS6ArcherPushupName": "Archer Push-up",
  "exercisePushS6ArcherPushupDesc": "Wide hand placement. Lower toward one arm while keeping the other arm straight. Alternate each side.",
  "exercisePushS6ArcherPushupTip": "Working arm goes full range; straight arm stays on the floor for support.",
  "exercisePushS7HandstandPushupName": "Handstand Push-up",
  "exercisePushS7HandstandPushupDesc": "Handstand against the wall (back to wall). Slowly lower your head toward the floor, then press your body back up.",
  "exercisePushS7HandstandPushupTip": "Spread your fingers wide for stability. Look between your hands.",
  "exerciseCoreS1CrunchesName": "Crunches",
  "exerciseCoreS1CrunchesDesc": "Lie on your back with knees bent. Hands behind your head or crossed on your chest. Lift your shoulder blades off the floor by contracting your abs.",
  "exerciseCoreS1CrunchesTip": "Don't pull your neck with your hands — pull your chest toward the ceiling.",
  "exerciseCoreS2PlankName": "Plank",
  "exerciseCoreS2PlankDesc": "Forearm push-up position. Body forms a straight line from heels to head. Don't raise your hips or arch your lower back.",
  "exerciseCoreS2PlankTip": "Brace your core and glutes. Breathe steadily — don't hold your breath.",
  "exerciseCoreS3LyingLegRaiseName": "Lying Leg Raise",
  "exerciseCoreS3LyingLegRaiseDesc": "Lie on your back with hands under your glutes. Raise straight legs to vertical, then lower them slowly without touching the floor.",
  "exerciseCoreS3LyingLegRaiseTip": "Keep your lower back pressed to the floor throughout the movement.",
  "exerciseCoreS4HangingLegRaiseName": "Hanging Leg Raise",
  "exerciseCoreS4HangingLegRaiseDesc": "Hang from a bar. Raise straight legs to parallel with the floor or higher. Control the descent.",
  "exerciseCoreS4HangingLegRaiseTip": "Don't swing — the movement comes from your abs only.",
  "exerciseCoreS4FlutterKicksName": "Flutter Kicks",
  "exerciseCoreS4FlutterKicksDesc": "Lie on your back, hands under your glutes. Lift both legs 15–20 cm off the floor. Alternate raising and lowering each leg in small quick movements. One rep = one cycle (right up + left up).",
  "exerciseCoreS4FlutterKicksTip": "Keep your lower back pressed to the floor. Legs don't touch the floor between reps.",
  "exerciseCoreS5LSitName": "L-sit",
  "exerciseCoreS5LSitDesc": "Support on parallel bars or the floor. Legs straight and parallel to the floor. Hold the position as long as possible.",
  "exerciseCoreS5LSitTip": "Point toes toward you; pull shoulders down and back.",
  "exerciseCoreS6DragonFlagName": "Dragon Flag",
  "exerciseCoreS6DragonFlagDesc": "Lie on a bench and grip a support behind your head. Lift your body into a straight line on your shoulder blades, then lower slowly.",
  "exerciseCoreS6DragonFlagTip": "Start with the negative phase (lowering only) — it's easier.",
  "exerciseWarmupArmRotationsName": "Arm Circles",
  "exerciseWarmupArmRotationsDesc": "Standing, make large circular movements with your arms forward and backward. Warms up the shoulder girdle before push-ups.",
  "exerciseWarmupJumpingJacksName": "Jumping Jacks",
  "exerciseWarmupJumpingJacksDesc": "Classic jumping jacks. Raises your heart rate and warms up your whole body in 30–60 seconds.",
  "exerciseCooldownShoulderStretchName": "Shoulder & Chest Stretch",
  "exerciseCooldownShoulderStretchDesc": "Clasp your hands behind your back and pull your shoulders back and down. Hold for 30 seconds.",
  "exerciseCooldownCatCowName": "Cat-Cow",
  "exerciseCooldownCatCowDesc": "On all fours: inhale and arch your back down (cow), exhale and round it up (cat). Releases tension in the lower back and abs.",
  "exercisePullS1AustralianName": "Australian Pull-up",
  "exercisePullS1AustralianDesc": "Lie under a bar with a slightly wider than shoulder-width grip. Pull your chest to the bar, keeping your body in a straight line. Control the descent.",
  "exercisePullS1AustralianTip": "The lower the bar, the harder the exercise.",
  "exercisePullS2NegativeName": "Negative Pull-up",
  "exercisePullS2NegativeDesc": "Jump up with your chin above the bar. Slowly lower yourself over 3–5 seconds until your arms are fully extended.",
  "exercisePullS2NegativeTip": "The slower you lower — the better. Aim for 5 seconds down.",
  "exercisePullS3PullupName": "Pull-up",
  "exercisePullS3PullupDesc": "Shoulder-width or slightly wider grip. Pull your chest to the bar until your chin is above it. Fully extend your arms at the bottom.",
  "exercisePullS3PullupTip": "Squeeze your shoulder blades — you're pulling with your back, not your arms.",
  "exercisePullS4CloseGripName": "Close-Grip Pull-up",
  "exercisePullS4CloseGripDesc": "Grip narrower than shoulder-width, palms facing you or away. Targets the biceps and lower lats. Pull your chest to the bar.",
  "exercisePullS4CloseGripTip": "Keep elbows tucked in for maximum bicep engagement.",
  "exercisePullS5ArcherName": "Archer Pull-up",
  "exercisePullS5ArcherDesc": "Wide grip. Pull your body toward one arm while keeping the other arm straight. Alternate each side.",
  "exercisePullS5ArcherTip": "Straight arm is for support; working arm goes full range.",
  "exercisePullS6OneArmName": "One-Arm Pull-up",
  "exercisePullS6OneArmDesc": "One hand on the bar, the other on your wrist or free. Full range of motion with the working arm.",
  "exercisePullS6OneArmTip": "Keep your core tight — don't swing.",
  "exerciseWarmupDeadHangName": "Dead Hang",
  "exerciseWarmupDeadHangDesc": "Hang from the bar with an overhand grip, arms fully extended. Relax your shoulders and hold the hang.",
  "exerciseCooldownLatStretchName": "Lat Stretch",
  "exerciseCooldownLatStretchDesc": "Stand sideways to a wall, raise one arm and press against it. Lean into the stretch to feel it along your side.",
  "exerciseLegsS1SquatName": "Squat",
  "exerciseLegsS1SquatDesc": "Feet shoulder-width apart, toes slightly turned out. Squat until thighs are parallel to the floor, knees over toes. Extend fully at the top.",
  "exerciseLegsS1SquatTip": "Keep heels on the floor and chest upright.",
  "exerciseLegsS2LungeName": "Lunge",
  "exerciseLegsS2LungeDesc": "Step forward and lower your back knee toward the floor without touching it. Both knees at 90°. Push off with the front foot to return.",
  "exerciseLegsS2LungeTip": "Keep your front knee behind your toes.",
  "exerciseLegsS3BulgarianName": "Bulgarian Split Squat",
  "exerciseLegsS3BulgarianDesc": "Rear foot elevated on a chair or couch. Lower your front leg until your thigh is parallel to the floor. Keep your torso upright.",
  "exerciseLegsS3BulgarianTip": "The further your front foot, the more glute activation.",
  "exerciseLegsS4AssistedPistolName": "Assisted Pistol Squat",
  "exerciseLegsS4AssistedPistolDesc": "Hold a door frame or pole for support. Squat on one leg while keeping the other straight in front of you. Use the support to reduce load.",
  "exerciseLegsS4AssistedPistolTip": "Gradually reduce hand assistance as you get stronger.",
  "exerciseLegsS5PistolName": "Pistol Squat",
  "exerciseLegsS5PistolDesc": "Single-leg squat without support. Other leg straight in front. Full range of motion to the floor and back up.",
  "exerciseLegsS5PistolTip": "Arms forward as a counterweight — it helps with balance.",
  "exerciseWarmupLegSwingsName": "Leg Swings",
  "exerciseWarmupLegSwingsDesc": "Standing by a wall, swing one leg forward and back, then side to side. Warms up the hip joint.",
  "exerciseCooldownQuadStretchName": "Quad Stretch",
  "exerciseCooldownQuadStretchDesc": "Stand on one leg, bend the other back and hold your foot with your hand. Feel the stretch along the front of your thigh.",
  "exerciseWarmupHipCirclesName": "Hip Circles",
  "exerciseWarmupHipCirclesDesc": "Stand with feet shoulder-width apart. Make slow circular movements with your hips clockwise then counter-clockwise. Warms up the hip joints.",
  "exerciseCooldownHipFlexorName": "Hip Flexor Stretch",
  "exerciseCooldownHipFlexorDesc": "Step into a lunge and lower your back knee to the floor. Press your hips forward and down to feel the stretch in your hip. Hold each side.",
  "exerciseBalS1OneLegStandName": "One-Leg Stand",
  "exerciseBalS1OneLegStandDesc": "Stand on one leg, keep the other slightly bent and off the ground. Arms can be out for balance.",
  "exerciseBalS1OneLegStandTip": "Fix your gaze on a point — it greatly improves balance.",
  "exerciseBalS2OneArmPlankName": "One-Arm Plank",
  "exerciseBalS2OneArmPlankDesc": "Classic straight-arm plank. Lift one hand off the floor and hold the position, body parallel to the floor.",
  "exerciseBalS2OneArmPlankTip": "Keep your hips parallel to the floor — don't rotate your torso.",
  "exerciseBalS3CrowPrepName": "Crow Pose Prep",
  "exerciseBalS3CrowPrepDesc": "Squat with knees on your triceps. Shift weight onto your hands, gently lifting your feet. Hold the balance.",
  "exerciseBalS3CrowPrepTip": "Look forward-down, not straight down — or you'll tip over.",
  "exerciseBalS4CrowPoseName": "Crow Pose (Kakasana)",
  "exerciseBalS4CrowPoseDesc": "Both knees on your triceps, full balance on your hands. Arms slightly bent, fingers spread wide.",
  "exerciseBalS4CrowPoseTip": "Round your back — it engages your core and provides balance.",
  "exerciseBalS5WallHsName": "Wall Handstand",
  "exerciseBalS5WallHsDesc": "Kick up into a handstand with your back to the wall. Heels touch the wall for support. Hold the position, body in a straight line.",
  "exerciseBalS5WallHsTip": "Spread fingers wide and press through the pads — that's your balance control.",
  "exerciseBalS6FreeHsName": "Free Handstand",
  "exerciseBalS6FreeHsDesc": "Handstand without wall support. Control balance with small finger and wrist movements.",
  "exerciseBalS6FreeHsTip": "Look at the floor 30–40 cm in front of your hands, not between them.",
  "exerciseWarmupWristCirclesName": "Wrist Circles",
  "exerciseWarmupWristCirclesDesc": "Rotate your wrists clockwise and counter-clockwise. Prepares your joints for weight-bearing on your hands.",
  "exerciseCooldownDownwardDogName": "Downward Dog",
  "exerciseCooldownDownwardDogDesc": "From all fours, straighten arms and legs and lift your hips up. Body forms an inverted V. Stretches wrists, shoulders, and legs.",
  "exerciseEveningBackS1CatCowName": "Cat-Cow",
  "exerciseEveningBackS1CatCowDesc": "On all fours, hands under your shoulders, knees under your hips. Breathing in, let your belly drop and lift your chest; breathing out, round your back toward the ceiling. Move slowly with your breath.",
  "exerciseEveningBackS1CatCowTip": "Let the breath lead: one slow breath in and one out per rep.",
  "exerciseEveningBackS2ChildsPoseName": "Child's Pose",
  "exerciseEveningBackS2ChildsPoseDesc": "Kneel with your big toes together and knees apart. Sit back on your heels and lay your chest down between your knees, arms stretched forward, forehead on the floor. Breathe into your back.",
  "exerciseEveningBackS2ChildsPoseTip": "Let your hips sink toward your heels with every breath out.",
  "exerciseEveningBackS3SupineTwistName": "Supine Twist",
  "exerciseEveningBackS3SupineTwistDesc": "Lie on your back, arms out to the sides. Bend one knee and let it fall across your body to the floor, looking the other way. Keep both shoulders down.",
  "exerciseEveningBackS3SupineTwistTip": "Don't push the knee down: the weight of the leg does the work.",
  "exerciseEveningBackS4SphinxName": "Sphinx",
  "exerciseEveningBackS4SphinxDesc": "Lie on your stomach, elbows under your shoulders, forearms on the floor. Lift your chest; your hips and legs stay relaxed on the floor.",
  "exerciseEveningBackS4SphinxTip": "Draw your shoulders away from your ears; the arch is gentle, never pinching.",
  "exerciseEveningBackS5CobraName": "Cobra",
  "exerciseEveningBackS5CobraDesc": "Lie on your stomach, hands under your shoulders. Press up and straighten your arms as far as your lower back allows; your hips stay on the floor.",
  "exerciseEveningBackS5CobraTip": "Keep the elbows soft and the shoulders down; stop where your back feels good.",
  "exerciseEveningHipsS1KneesToChestName": "Knees to Chest",
  "exerciseEveningHipsS1KneesToChestDesc": "Lie on your back, hug both knees to your chest and hold. You may rock gently from side to side.",
  "exerciseEveningHipsS1KneesToChestTip": "Keep your lower back and your head on the floor.",
  "exerciseEveningHipsS2FigureFourName": "Reclined Figure Four",
  "exerciseEveningHipsS2FigureFourDesc": "Lie on your back, knees bent. Cross one ankle over the other knee, then pull that thigh toward your chest until you feel the stretch in the buttock.",
  "exerciseEveningHipsS2FigureFourTip": "Press the crossed knee gently away from you to go deeper.",
  "exerciseEveningHipsS3HappyBabyName": "Happy Baby",
  "exerciseEveningHipsS3HappyBabyDesc": "Lie on your back, bring your knees toward your armpits and hold the outer edges of your feet, soles to the ceiling. Gently pull your knees toward the floor.",
  "exerciseEveningHipsS3HappyBabyTip": "Keep your tailbone down; rocking a little is fine.",
  "exerciseEveningHipsS4ButterflyName": "Butterfly",
  "exerciseEveningHipsS4ButterflyDesc": "Sit up tall with the soles of your feet together and your knees out to the sides. Hold your feet and let your knees sink toward the floor.",
  "exerciseEveningHipsS4ButterflyTip": "Stay tall; to go deeper, lean forward from your hips.",
  "exerciseEveningHipsS5FrogName": "Frog",
  "exerciseEveningHipsS5FrogDesc": "On all fours, slide your knees wide apart, ankles in line with the knees, feet turned out. Lower onto your forearms and ease your hips back.",
  "exerciseEveningHipsS5FrogTip": "Open only as far as it feels like a stretch, never a pain in the knees.",
  "exerciseEveningFoldsS1LegsUpWallName": "Legs Up the Wall",
  "exerciseEveningFoldsS1LegsUpWallDesc": "Lie on your back with your hips close to a wall and your legs straight up along it. Arms relaxed at your sides; breathe slowly.",
  "exerciseEveningFoldsS1LegsUpWallTip": "Bend your knees a little if the backs of your legs pull too much.",
  "exerciseEveningFoldsS2TowelHamstringName": "Lying Hamstring Stretch",
  "exerciseEveningFoldsS2TowelHamstringDesc": "Lie on your back, loop a towel around one foot and raise that leg as straight as you can. The other leg stays on the floor.",
  "exerciseEveningFoldsS2TowelHamstringTip": "Pull with the towel, not with your back: your hips stay on the floor.",
  "exerciseEveningFoldsS3HeadToKneeName": "Head-to-Knee Fold",
  "exerciseEveningFoldsS3HeadToKneeDesc": "Sit with one leg straight and the other foot against the inside of that thigh. Fold forward over the straight leg, reaching toward the foot.",
  "exerciseEveningFoldsS3HeadToKneeTip": "Lead with your chest, not your head; the straight knee may bend a little.",
  "exerciseEveningFoldsS4StraddleFoldName": "Straddle Fold",
  "exerciseEveningFoldsS4StraddleFoldDesc": "Sit with your legs wide apart, knees pointing up. Walk your hands forward and lower your body toward the floor between your legs.",
  "exerciseEveningFoldsS4StraddleFoldTip": "Tilt from your hips with a long back; rounding the back adds nothing.",
  "exerciseEveningShouldersS1SelfHugName": "Self-Hug",
  "exerciseEveningShouldersS1SelfHugDesc": "Sitting or standing, wrap your arms around yourself and hold your shoulder blades. Let your upper back round and breathe into it.",
  "exerciseEveningShouldersS1SelfHugTip": "Relax your neck and let your chin drop a little.",
  "exerciseEveningShouldersS2TricepsStretchName": "Overhead Triceps Stretch",
  "exerciseEveningShouldersS2TricepsStretchDesc": "Raise one arm, bend the elbow and let your hand drop behind your neck. Use the other hand to ease the elbow back.",
  "exerciseEveningShouldersS2TricepsStretchTip": "Keep your head up and your ribs down.",
  "exerciseEveningShouldersS3EagleArmsName": "Eagle Arms",
  "exerciseEveningShouldersS3EagleArmsDesc": "Cross one arm under the other at the elbows, bend them and bring your palms together. Lift your elbows to shoulder height.",
  "exerciseEveningShouldersS3EagleArmsTip": "If your palms don't meet, press the backs of your hands together.",
  "exerciseEveningShouldersS4PuppyPoseName": "Puppy Pose",
  "exerciseEveningShouldersS4PuppyPoseDesc": "On all fours, walk your hands forward and lower your chest toward the floor, hips above your knees, arms straight.",
  "exerciseEveningShouldersS4PuppyPoseTip": "Rest your forehead on the floor and let your chest melt down.",
  "exerciseEveningShouldersS5CowFaceArmsName": "Cow Face Arms",
  "exerciseEveningShouldersS5CowFaceArmsDesc": "Reach one hand down behind your neck and the other up behind your back, and try to hook your fingers. If they don't meet, hold a towel between your hands.",
  "exerciseEveningShouldersS5CowFaceArmsTip": "Keep the upper elbow pointing up and your back straight.",
  "exerciseCooldownLyingRelaxationName": "Lying Relaxation",
  "exerciseCooldownLyingRelaxationDesc": "Lie on your back, arms by your sides, palms up. Close your eyes and breathe slowly; let your whole body go heavy.",
  "exerciseCooldownLyingRelaxationTip": "Breathe out longer than you breathe in.",
  "exerciseMorningSpineS1SideBendName": "Standing Side Bend",
  "exerciseMorningSpineS1SideBendDesc": "Stand with your feet hip-width apart. Raise one arm over your head and lean to the other side, sliding the other hand down your thigh. Come back up and switch sides. Each side counts as one rep.",
  "exerciseMorningSpineS1SideBendTip": "Lean straight to the side, not forward; your hips stay still.",
  "exerciseMorningSpineS2TorsoTwistName": "Torso Twist",
  "exerciseMorningSpineS2TorsoTwistDesc": "Stand with your feet a little wider than your hips, knees soft, arms loose. Turn your upper body from side to side and let your arms swing around you. Your hips keep facing forward. Each side counts as one rep.",
  "exerciseMorningSpineS2TorsoTwistTip": "Let the arms follow the turn; don't throw them.",
  "exerciseMorningSpineS3GoodMorningName": "Good Morning",
  "exerciseMorningSpineS3GoodMorningDesc": "Stand with your feet hip-width apart, hands behind your head. Push your hips back and lean forward with a flat back until you feel the back of your thighs, then stand tall again.",
  "exerciseMorningSpineS3GoodMorningTip": "Bend at the hips, not at the waist: your back stays straight the whole way.",
  "exerciseMorningSpineS4RollDownName": "Roll-Down",
  "exerciseMorningSpineS4RollDownDesc": "Stand tall. Drop your chin to your chest and roll down slowly, one vertebra at a time, letting your arms hang toward the floor. Roll back up the same way, your head coming up last.",
  "exerciseMorningSpineS4RollDownTip": "Bend your knees as much as you need; the point is the spine, not touching the floor.",
  "exerciseMorningSpineS5WindmillName": "Windmill",
  "exerciseMorningSpineS5WindmillDesc": "Stand with your feet wide, arms out to the sides. Bend forward and turn, reaching one hand to the opposite foot while the other arm points at the ceiling. Come back up to the T and switch sides. Each side counts as one rep.",
  "exerciseMorningSpineS5WindmillTip": "Keep both arms in one straight line, like the sails of a windmill.",
  "exerciseMorningJointsS1KneeCirclesName": "Knee Circles",
  "exerciseMorningJointsS1KneeCirclesDesc": "Stand with your feet together, bend your knees slightly and rest your hands just above them. Draw slow circles with your knees: half of them one way, half the other.",
  "exerciseMorningJointsS1KneeCirclesTip": "Small, smooth circles; your heels stay on the floor.",
  "exerciseMorningJointsS2OpenTheGateName": "Open the Gate",
  "exerciseMorningJointsS2OpenTheGateDesc": "Stand tall. Lift one knee in front of you to hip height, open it out to the side and lower the foot back down. Switch legs. Each side counts as one rep.",
  "exerciseMorningJointsS2OpenTheGateTip": "Hold on to a wall or a chair if you wobble; keep your chest up.",
  "exerciseMorningJointsS3KneeHugName": "Standing Knee Hug",
  "exerciseMorningJointsS3KneeHugDesc": "Stand tall. Pull one knee to your chest with both hands and rise onto the toes of the standing foot. Lower it and switch legs. Each side counts as one rep.",
  "exerciseMorningJointsS3KneeHugTip": "Rise slowly and look at a point in front of you to keep your balance.",
  "exerciseMorningJointsS4SideLungeName": "Side Lunge",
  "exerciseMorningJointsS4SideLungeDesc": "Stand with your feet together. Step wide to one side and sit back into that hip, the other leg straight, both feet flat on the floor. Push back to the start and switch sides. Each side counts as one rep.",
  "exerciseMorningJointsS4SideLungeTip": "Your bent knee points the same way as your toes.",
  "exerciseMorningJointsS5CossackSquatName": "Cossack Squat",
  "exerciseMorningJointsS5CossackSquatDesc": "Stand with your feet very wide. Sink deep onto one leg while the other stays straight, toes pointing up. Move through the middle to the other side. Each side counts as one rep.",
  "exerciseMorningJointsS5CossackSquatTip": "Keep the heel of the bent leg down; reach your arms forward for balance.",
  "exerciseMorningArmsS1ArmSwingsName": "Arm Swings",
  "exerciseMorningArmsS1ArmSwingsDesc": "Stand tall. Open your arms wide to the sides, then swing them in and hug yourself, changing which arm is on top each time. Keep it loose and easy.",
  "exerciseMorningArmsS1ArmSwingsTip": "Open your chest at the wide point and breathe in.",
  "exerciseMorningArmsS2YRaisesName": "Y Raises",
  "exerciseMorningArmsS2YRaisesDesc": "Knees soft, lean forward from the hips with a flat back. Thumbs up, raise your straight arms forward and up into a Y, squeezing your shoulder blades, then lower them.",
  "exerciseMorningArmsS2YRaisesTip": "Lift with the shoulder blades, not by arching your lower back.",
  "exerciseMorningArmsS3CactusArmsName": "Cactus Arms",
  "exerciseMorningArmsS3CactusArmsDesc": "Raise your arms to the sides, elbows at shoulder height and bent at 90°, forearms pointing up like a cactus. Keeping the elbows in place, turn your forearms forward and down until they point at the floor, then back up, squeezing your shoulder blades.",
  "exerciseMorningArmsS3CactusArmsTip": "Move slowly: only the forearms travel, the elbows stay at shoulder height.",
  "exerciseMorningArmsS4InchwormName": "Inchworm",
  "exerciseMorningArmsS4InchwormDesc": "Stand tall, bend forward and put your hands on the floor (bend your knees if you need to). Walk your hands out to a plank, then walk them back to your feet and roll up to standing.",
  "exerciseMorningArmsS4InchwormTip": "In the plank, keep your body in one straight line.",
  "exerciseMorningArmsS5PlankToDogName": "Plank to Downward Dog",
  "exerciseMorningArmsS5PlankToDogDesc": "Start in a high plank, hands under your shoulders. Push your hips up and back into an upside-down V, heels toward the floor, then lower back to the plank.",
  "exerciseMorningArmsS5PlankToDogTip": "Push the floor away with your hands and let your head hang between your arms.",
  "exerciseMorningEnergyS1StepJacksName": "Step Jacks",
  "exerciseMorningEnergyS1StepJacksDesc": "Jumping jacks without the jump: step one foot out to the side as both arms go up over your head, bring it back as the arms come down, then the other foot. Keep a steady rhythm.",
  "exerciseMorningEnergyS1StepJacksTip": "Stay light on your feet and never jump, so nobody wakes up.",
  "exerciseMorningEnergyS2ButtKicksName": "Butt Kicks",
  "exerciseMorningEnergyS2ButtKicksDesc": "On the spot, kick one heel up toward your glutes, then the other, at a brisk pace. Arms bent, swinging with your legs. One foot always stays on the floor.",
  "exerciseMorningEnergyS2ButtKicksTip": "Quiet steps on the balls of your feet: brisk, but no jumping.",
  "exerciseMorningEnergyS3CrossCrunchName": "Standing Cross Crunch",
  "exerciseMorningEnergyS3CrossCrunchDesc": "Stand with your hands behind your head. Lift one knee and bring the opposite elbow down to meet it, then switch sides, at a steady pace.",
  "exerciseMorningEnergyS3CrossCrunchTip": "Turn from the waist and open your chest between reps.",
  "exerciseMorningEnergyS4SpeedSkaterName": "Speed Skater",
  "exerciseMorningEnergyS4SpeedSkaterDesc": "Like a skater, but without the hop: step wide to one side onto a bent leg and sweep the other foot behind it, swinging the opposite arm across your body. Then step to the other side.",
  "exerciseMorningEnergyS4SpeedSkaterTip": "Sink into the standing leg and keep your chest over it.",
  "exerciseMorningEnergyS5MountainClimbersName": "Slow Mountain Climbers",
  "exerciseMorningEnergyS5MountainClimbersDesc": "In a high plank, hands under your shoulders, bring one knee toward your chest and put the foot back, then the other. A steady pace, no jumping from foot to foot.",
  "exerciseMorningEnergyS5MountainClimbersTip": "Hips level with your shoulders; don't let them pop up.",
  "exerciseWarmupMorningStretchUpName": "Morning Stretch-Up",
  "exerciseWarmupMorningStretchUpDesc": "Stand tall. Breathing in, reach both arms up over your head and rise onto your toes; breathing out, lower your heels and arms. Stretch as if you have just woken up.",
  "exerciseWarmupMorningStretchUpTip": "Reach long through your fingertips; wake up slowly.",
  "exerciseCooldownShakeOutName": "Shake-Out",
  "exerciseCooldownShakeOutDesc": "Stand loosely and shake out your hands, arms and legs, bouncing softly in your knees. Finish with a deep breath: the day can begin.",
  "exerciseCooldownShakeOutTip": "Let everything hang loose: wrists, shoulders, jaw.",
  "exerciseYogaStandingS1ChairName": "Chair Pose",
  "exerciseYogaStandingS1ChairDesc": "Feet together, bend your knees and sit back as if onto a chair, arms raised alongside your ears. Weight in your heels, chest lifted.",
  "exerciseYogaStandingS1ChairTip": "Keep your knees behind your toes and draw your belly in.",
  "exerciseYogaStandingS2Warrior1Name": "Warrior I",
  "exerciseYogaStandingS2Warrior1Desc": "Step one foot far back and turn it out slightly, bend the front knee over the ankle, hips facing forward. Raise both arms overhead. Then the other side.",
  "exerciseYogaStandingS2Warrior1Tip": "Press the back heel into the floor and keep the back leg straight.",
  "exerciseYogaStandingS3Warrior2Name": "Warrior II",
  "exerciseYogaStandingS3Warrior2Desc": "Feet wide apart, the front foot pointing forward, the back foot turned in. Bend the front knee over the ankle and stretch your arms out to the sides at shoulder height, gaze over the front hand. Then the other side.",
  "exerciseYogaStandingS3Warrior2Tip": "The front knee points over your middle toes, not inward.",
  "exerciseYogaStandingS4TriangleName": "Triangle Pose",
  "exerciseYogaStandingS4TriangleDesc": "Feet wide, the front foot pointing forward. With both legs straight, reach forward and tip your torso over the front leg: the lower hand rests on the shin, the upper arm points at the ceiling. Then the other side.",
  "exerciseYogaStandingS4TriangleTip": "Lengthen both sides of your waist; don't sink onto the front leg.",
  "exerciseYogaStandingS5SideAngleName": "Extended Side Angle",
  "exerciseYogaStandingS5SideAngleDesc": "From Warrior II, rest the forearm of your front arm on the front thigh (or the hand on the floor) and reach the other arm over your ear: one long line from the back foot to the fingertips. Then the other side.",
  "exerciseYogaStandingS5SideAngleTip": "Keep the front knee over the ankle and turn your chest toward the ceiling.",
  "exerciseYogaOneLegS1TreeName": "Tree Pose",
  "exerciseYogaOneLegS1TreeDesc": "Stand on one leg and place the other foot on the inner calf or thigh (never on the knee), the knee out to the side. Hands together at the chest or raised overhead. Then the other side.",
  "exerciseYogaOneLegS1TreeTip": "Fix your gaze on one point and press the foot and the leg into each other.",
  "exerciseYogaOneLegS2EagleName": "Eagle Pose",
  "exerciseYogaOneLegS2EagleDesc": "Bend your knees, cross one thigh over the other and hook the foot behind the standing calf if you can. Cross the arms at the elbows, palms together in front of your face. Sit a little deeper. Then the other side.",
  "exerciseYogaOneLegS2EagleTip": "Keep your hips square and lift the elbows to shoulder height.",
  "exerciseYogaOneLegS3Warrior3Name": "Warrior III",
  "exerciseYogaOneLegS3Warrior3Desc": "Stand on one leg, hinge forward and lift the other leg behind you until your body and the leg form a T, arms reaching forward. Then the other side.",
  "exerciseYogaOneLegS3Warrior3Tip": "Keep both hips level and the standing knee soft.",
  "exerciseYogaOneLegS4DancerName": "Dancer Pose",
  "exerciseYogaOneLegS4DancerDesc": "Stand on one leg, take the other foot behind you with the hand on the same side and press the foot into the hand: the leg rises, the torso tips forward, the free arm reaches ahead. Then the other side.",
  "exerciseYogaOneLegS4DancerTip": "Press the foot back into the hand rather than pulling the leg up.",
  "exerciseYogaOneLegS5HalfMoonName": "Half Moon",
  "exerciseYogaOneLegS5HalfMoonDesc": "Tip sideways over one leg: the lower hand on the floor (or a block) under the shoulder, the other leg lifted level with your body, the upper arm pointing at the ceiling. Then the other side.",
  "exerciseYogaOneLegS5HalfMoonTip": "Stack the hips and shoulders as if your back were against a wall.",
  "exerciseYogaBackbendsS2LocustName": "Locust Pose",
  "exerciseYogaBackbendsS2LocustDesc": "Lie on your stomach, arms along your body, palms down. Lift your chest, arms and legs off the floor at the same time, gazing down and slightly forward.",
  "exerciseYogaBackbendsS2LocustTip": "Lengthen through your legs instead of squeezing your lower back.",
  "exerciseYogaBackbendsS3BridgeName": "Bridge Pose",
  "exerciseYogaBackbendsS3BridgeDesc": "Lie on your back, knees bent, feet hip-width apart near your hips. Press into your feet and lift your hips as high as you can, arms on the floor. Hold, then roll down one vertebra at a time.",
  "exerciseYogaBackbendsS3BridgeTip": "Knees point forward, not out; squeeze your glutes.",
  "exerciseYogaBackbendsS4BowName": "Bow Pose",
  "exerciseYogaBackbendsS4BowDesc": "Lie on your stomach, bend your knees and hold your ankles from the outside. Press the feet into your hands to lift your chest and thighs: the body curves like a bow.",
  "exerciseYogaBackbendsS4BowTip": "Keep your knees no wider than your hips.",
  "exerciseYogaBackbendsS5CamelName": "Camel Pose",
  "exerciseYogaBackbendsS5CamelDesc": "Kneel with your knees hip-width apart, toes tucked, hands on your lower back. Press your hips forward, lift the chest and arch back, the head following gently. Come up chest first.",
  "exerciseYogaBackbendsS5CamelTip": "Keep your hips over your knees; the arch comes from the chest, not the lower back.",
  "exerciseYogaBackbendsS6WheelName": "Wheel Pose",
  "exerciseYogaBackbendsS6WheelDesc": "Lie on your back, knees bent, feet near your hips, hands planted by your shoulders. Lift your hips, then press up through the hands until the arms straighten and the head hangs between them. Lower slowly, chin to the chest.",
  "exerciseYogaBackbendsS6WheelTip": "Keep your feet parallel and push the floor away evenly with hands and feet.",
  "exerciseYogaFlowS3HalfSunSalutationName": "Half Sun Salutation",
  "exerciseYogaFlowS3HalfSunSalutationDesc": "One round: standing, sweep the arms up, fold forward, lift halfway with a flat back, fold again, rise with the arms up and lower them. Move with your breath.",
  "exerciseYogaFlowS3HalfSunSalutationTip": "Breathe in as you rise, out as you fold.",
  "exerciseYogaFlowS4SunSalutationAName": "Sun Salutation A",
  "exerciseYogaFlowS4SunSalutationADesc": "One round: arms up, fold, half lift, step back to a plank, lower halfway, upward dog, downward dog for a few breaths, step forward, half lift, rise with the arms up, stand.",
  "exerciseYogaFlowS4SunSalutationATip": "One movement per breath; drop your knees to lower if you need to.",
  "exerciseYogaFlowS5SunSalutationBName": "Sun Salutation B",
  "exerciseYogaFlowS5SunSalutationBDesc": "Like Sun Salutation A, with Chair Pose at the start and the end and Warrior I on each side: chair, fold, plank, lower, upward dog, downward dog, Warrior I on one side, back through the plank to downward dog, Warrior I on the other side, then forward to the chair.",
  "exerciseYogaFlowS5SunSalutationBTip": "Keep your breath even: it sets the pace.",
